course: dictionary
lesson: 7459
title: One word, two poppies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word poppy is a good example. Read the words around it and ask: is this a plant, a paper flower, or a name?
explain: «the red poppy with a black centre for remembering the dead of the Second World War» Here the clue is remembering the dead. People wear a poppy to remember soldiers, so this poppy is a red paper or fabric flower, not a plant growing in a field.
explain: «Poppy hugs her new bunny and announces» Look at the capital P in the middle of a sentence. Poppy is the name of a girl, so it is not a flower at all. Capital letters in the middle of a sentence often mean a name.
explain: «Poppies grow in disturbed soil, so they come up on fields and roadsides after digging.» Here grow and soil are the clues: this poppy is a living plant. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A poppy is a plant with large, soft, usually bright red flowers and a dark centre.
fact: A poppy can also be a red paper or fabric flower, worn to remember soldiers who died in wars.
fact: Poppies grow in disturbed soil, so they come up on fields and roadsides after digging.
fact: The seed head of a poppy shakes out seeds through a ring of little holes, like a pepper pot.
fact: Poppy seeds are used in food too: «kutYa» is sweet wheat with poppy seeds, honey and nuts, eaten at the Christmas Eve dinner.
exercise: «Poppies grow in disturbed soil, so they come up on fields and roadsides after digging.» What is a poppy in this sentence? | A person's name | A type of bread | A soldier | *A plant
exercise: «Poppy hugs her new bunny and announces, "Snowy's getting a carrot every single day!"» What is Poppy in this sentence? | A plant with red flowers | *A girl's name | A red paper flower | A kind of seed
exercise: People in the UK wear a red paper poppy on Remembrance Day. Why? | To prove they have dug a garden | To keep the rain off | To show they have a new pet | *To remember soldiers who died in wars
test: «kutYa is sweet wheat with poppy seeds, honey and nuts, eaten at the Christmas Eve dinner.» What are the poppy seeds? | The name of a Christmas dish | A kind of nut | Red paper flowers worn on a coat | *Tiny seeds from the poppy plant
test: «the red poppy with a black centre for remembering the dead of the Second World War» Which meaning fits best? | *A red paper or fabric flower worn to remember soldiers | A plant that grows on fields | A kind of wheat | A girl's name
exam: Look at «Poppy hugs her new bunny and announces...». What is the best meaning of Poppy here? | A seed from a seed head | A plant with red flowers and a dark centre | *A girl's name, because of the capital P | A paper flower worn in November
